g time  loops two re-zero did and it's my pick  for 2016's top mystery series it's a  really close battle between that and  erased and ultimately i give re-zero the  nod primarily an isakai and a thriller  re zero builds most of its intrigue by  shooting us into a world full of  questions that need to be answered  what's the nature of subaru's loops  what's rosewall really like what's  amelia's relation to the witches as a  series it thrives on building suspicion  and slowly lifting the veil one painful  loop at a time  this gives the show such an engaging  narrative that i just couldn't get  enough of the anime fans seem to agree  as re zero has quickly become one of the  most beloved and popular isakai series  of them all  2017.  coming off the high of the 2016 season  my expectations were sky high for 2017.  for the most part i wasn't disappointed  because 2017 gave us some of the most  unique and renowned mystery anime in  recent memory in quick enumeration we  have acca princess principal land of the  lustrous and girls last tour with such a  wide selection you get your fair share  of politics action and sci-fi scattered  amongst the mentioned shows however  there's one mystery anime this year that  stands above the lot of them and that's  the critically acclaimed made in abyss  what i absolutely love about made in  abyss is that it's pretty much got the  best of all worlds character dynamics an  absolutely enthralling world waiting to  be explored beautifully drawn  backgrounds and the ability to shift  seamlessly from light-hearted to serious  the series has it all if you're someone  who's quite used to anime and the  general ins and outs of the medium this  is a show that i can readily recommend  as the good far outweighs the possibly  questionable content in it i won't call  it an adventure story that can be  enjoyed by the entire family but if  you're up for a thrilling journey  complete with an emotional rollercoaster  that can be as dark and batshit crazy as  anime goes then you are in luck made in  abyss is my pick for this year and i  think it will be yours too  2018.  unfortunately 2018 happened to be quite  a thin year for mystery anime relatively  speaking it's not that there's an  absolute shortage of mystery shows  however i don't have a lot of memorable  ones that i've seen especially when put  against the year we just had 2017.  experience only tells part of the story  and i'd like your help to give me some  suggestions for non-sequel mystery anime  series or films that began in 2018.  however though it isn't all doom and  gloom before the upcoming uzumaki junji  ito collection aired this year providing  the much-awaited grotesque horror edge  that the mystery anime i've talked about  have mostly lacked this one is more of a  pure horror thing compared to something  like tokyo ghoul after all i also  enjoyed be the beginning from this year  i'm always down for psychological  thrillers and had a good time watching  this vigilante series that surprisingly  provides a lot of interesting nuggets  about morals corruption and loyalty for  this year though i give the crown to a  chinese anime modal sushi those of you  into live action would have probably  heard of the series through the hit  drama the untamed but the anime  adaptation i'd say provides a really  great adaptation of the popular web  novel as well taking us to an ancient  world of dark arts and magic modauzushi  gives us a healthy dose of fights drama  and adventure as our two main characters  move to unravel the mysteries of the  spiritual world  2019  for me 2019's notable for one show my  pick for 2019's mystery anime of the  year is the horror thriller show the  promised neverland it truly set the bar  for excellence in horror and suspense  and it's amazing because the main source  of the horror is not even the demons  they come in the form of the sound  direction presentation the camera cuts  and all of that sort of stuff the  promise neverland