 to be a serious live-action  crime drama it also has a lot of  well-written characters that avoid or  subvert the usual tropes that you see in  the medium so yeah stop calling it a  poor man's derivative of psychopaths and  give id invaded a shot it's definitely  going to be worth your time 2021  if you've been listening to a lot of  antitubers these days no doubt you've  heard of the name or taxi people can't  stop talking about it and a lot of them  are pretty much getting ready to hand  the anime of the year title 2 or taxi do  you think that it deserves anime of the  year i mean i'm personally not as ready  to crowd it just yet but it does make  for a very strong case which is why  despite having one more season to go i'm  pretty confident that odd taxi is going  to retain its crown of being 2021's  mystery anime of the year what makes odd  taxi so unique is how deceptively simple  it seems honestly i feel that any random  passerby seeing the poster would  probably not feel as inclined to go for  it it's a show whose viewership seems to  be carried by word of mouth but really  it does deserve all the praise it's  deceptively simple and light but what  you'll get from one taxi is a very  immersive set of mysteries that just  keep building aided by the strong  writing you won't get bored as each  character has their own story to tell  and a contribution to the grand finale  that everything is building up to as for  other contenders i'd give them to kimono  gn sony boy and the chinese anime link  click they're great anime in their own  ways but i don't think that they come  anywhere close to our taxi if we were to  look at them as purely mysteries kimono  gn does have the stronger mass appeal  factor but it falls just a bit short  compared to odd taxi almost everywhere  else  that more or less wraps it up so how did  my list compare with yours if you like  watching the video and want to support  the channel in a more direct method you  might want to consider my pa